cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Knap in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Knap: a pure Mojo byte level BPE tokenizer"
abstract: >-
  Knap is a byte level Byte Pair Encoding tokenizer written in pure Mojo,
  built to produce byte identical output to tiktoken on arbitrary input.
  Its stated goals, in order, are exact parity with the reference
  implementation, a SIMD pre-tokenizer usable as a standalone module, and a
  Python free tokenization path for Mojo and MAX applications. Raw merge
  speed is explicitly not a goal, because the BPE merge loop does not
  vectorize and the established Rust implementations are already fast.
type: software
authors:
